# Booking — Availability Alerts (M23-S06, UC-072 / UC-076)
# TenantContext populated from X-Tenant-ID / X-Actor-ID headers (set by BFF).
# CUSTOMER only — STAFF, MANAGER and guests get 403. Every route acts on the caller's own alerts;
# another customer's alert (same tenant) and another tenant's alert both answer 404.
# An alert is an intent only: it reserves nothing and never books. Its timezone is always the
# tenant's. It expires 30 days after creation unless "expiresAt" is sent (at most 90 days after
# creation; for a ONE_TIME_RANGE it is clamped to "acceptableEndAt"). At most 10 ACTIVE alerts per
# customer (409 BOOKING_ALERT_CAP_REACHED); the service must have availabilityAlertEligible = true
# (422 BOOKING_ALERT_INELIGIBLE_SERVICE).
#
# Prerequisites:
#   1. pnpm infra:up
#   2. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run migration:run
#   3. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run dev
#
# REST Client environment: select "local" in VS Code status bar

@baseUrl = {{backendUrl}}
@alertId = {{createWeeklyAlert.response.body.id}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HAPPY PATH — create, list, edit, cancel
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Create a weekly-preference alert ("Tuesdays and Thursdays, 18:00–20:00")
# @name createWeeklyAlert
POST {{baseUrl}}/availability-alerts
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "criteriaType": "WEEKLY_PREFERENCE",
  "weekdays": ["tuesday", "thursday"],
  "localStartTime": "18:00",
  "localEndTime": "20:00",
  "durationMinutes": 120,
  "participantCount": 2
}

###

### Create a one-time-range alert for a preferred resource
POST {{baseUrl}}/availability-alerts
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "preferredResourceId": "{{resourceId}}",
  "criteriaType": "ONE_TIME_RANGE",
  "acceptableStartAt": "2026-10-12T14:00:00.000Z",
  "acceptableEndAt": "2026-10-12T18:00:00.000Z"
}

###

### List my alerts (newest first, history included)
GET {{baseUrl}}/availability-alerts
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER

###

### Read one of my alerts by id, whatever its status or age (M23-S42) — 404 BOOKING_ALERT_NOT_FOUND
### for another customer's alert or another tenant's
GET {{baseUrl}}/availability-alerts/{{alertId}}
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER

###

### Edit an alert — change only the weekdays (merged over the current criteria)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/availability-alerts/{{alertId}}
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "weekdays": ["friday"]
}

###

### Edit an alert — switch to a one-time range (the full new set is required)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/availability-alerts/{{alertId}}
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "criteriaType": "ONE_TIME_RANGE",
  "acceptableStartAt": "2026-10-14T14:00:00.000Z",
  "acceptableEndAt": "2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z"
}

###

### Cancel an alert (idempotent; a notified or expired alert answers 409)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/availability-alerts/{{alertId}}
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ERROR PATHS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 422 — both criteria representations (range fields on a weekly alert)
POST {{baseUrl}}/availability-alerts
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "criteriaType": "WEEKLY_PREFERENCE",
  "weekdays": ["monday"],
  "localStartTime": "09:00",
  "localEndTime": "10:00",
  "acceptableStartAt": "2026-10-12T14:00:00.000Z"
}

###

### 422 BOOKING_DURATION_OUT_OF_RANGE — customer-selected-duration service with no valid duration
# {{variableServiceId}} is a service with durationPolicy CUSTOMER_SELECTED; omit durationMinutes or send one off its min/max/increment.
POST {{baseUrl}}/availability-alerts
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{variableServiceId}}",
  "criteriaType": "WEEKLY_PREFERENCE",
  "weekdays": ["monday"],
  "localStartTime": "09:00",
  "localEndTime": "10:00"
}

###

### Create an alert on a customer-selected-duration service with a valid duration (the PATCH below edits it)
# @name createVariableAlert
POST {{baseUrl}}/availability-alerts
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{variableServiceId}}",
  "criteriaType": "WEEKLY_PREFERENCE",
  "weekdays": ["monday"],
  "localStartTime": "09:00",
  "localEndTime": "10:00",
  "durationMinutes": 60
}

###

### 422 BOOKING_DURATION_OUT_OF_RANGE — PATCH clearing the duration of that active alert
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/availability-alerts/{{createVariableAlert.response.body.id}}
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{ "durationMinutes": null }

###

### 403 — a STAFF actor cannot use alerts
GET {{baseUrl}}/availability-alerts
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{staffId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: STAFF
